  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Online Bureau\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Aug 27, 2026 at 02:28 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: <a href=\"/tag/fortis+hospitals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fortis Hospitals</a> in Shalimar Bagh and Vasant Kunj have launched dedicated <a href=\"/tag/lung+failure+clinics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">lung failure clinics</a> to offer care for patients suffering from advanced and end-stage lung diseases.The corporate hospital chain said the clinics will focus on the management of advanced lung failure, including evaluation for lung transplantation, and provide patients with access to multidisciplinary, end-to-end <a href=\"/tag/respiratory+care\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">respiratory care</a>.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>This includes pre and post-transplant care coordination, pulmonary rehabilitation, and access to advanced diagnostics such as bronchoscopy, sleep evaluation and non-invasive ventilation support.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>The clinics will be led by Dr Govini Balasubramani, Director, Lung Transplant and Advanced Lung Failure, Gleneagles Hospital Chennai, Dr Vikas Maurya, Senior Director and HOD, Respiratory Medicine and Respiratory Critical Care, Fortis Hospital Shalimar Bagh; and Dr Prashant Saxena, Principal Director and Head, Pulmonology, Critical Care and Sleep Medicine, Fortis Hospital Vasant Kunj.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The move comes amid deteriorating air quality in the Delhi NCR region and a rising demand for specialised respiratory care.Air pollution is increasingly being linked to a rise in severe respiratory, cardiovascular, and systemic diseases.</p><p>As per a recent study published in the journal of Natural Health, PM2.5 emerged as the dominant contributor to the global cancer burden, accounting for approximately 8.82 million attributable cases during the study period,\" they said.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>About 17.9 per cent of tracheal, bronchial and lung cancer cases could be prevented if exposure to PM2.5 was removed or addressed, the study found.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Aug 27, 2026 at 02:28 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Aug 27, 2026 at 02:28 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                                            <!-- <div class=\"app-store-container desktop-view\">\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"\" aria-label=\"Play Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-g-play.png\" alt=\"\" />\n                            </a>\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"App Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons